     1	"""CP-5 cross-engine integration battery (E10 Momentum / E11 Regime / E12 Temporal).
     2
     3	Closes the CP-5 EXIT-box items that span engines:
     4
     5	  - **E07 ↔ E12 integration, BOTH modes** — the CP-4 degraded branch
     6	    (``E12_UNAVAILABLE_DEGRADED_QX``, NON-authoritative local registry, Q-cap)
     7	    is re-proven side-by-side with the RESOLVED branch driven by the real
     8	    ``E12TemporalProvider`` (``E12_Temporal_Context.Contract v4.0.0``,
     9	    ``config_version=v2024a``, §3.5 canonical registry, §3.7 Q5 reachable
    10	    only on the authoritative overlap flag).  A failing provider still fails
    11	    closed into the degraded branch.
    12	  - **E11 live-regime gate** — default OFF (Phase-7 + Owner approval,
    13	    AI.2 L19046–48); the flag never appears inside regime_state (§5.1
    14	    additionalProperties:false) and the engine never self-enables.
    15	  - **E11 Wave-Out** — next-regime forecasting raises ``WaveOutError``.
    16	  - **T-DR-001** re-run for all three CP-5 engines over one shared window.
    17	  - **Emission rows** for E10/E11/E12 validate against the frozen store DDL.
